## AI Assistance Disclosure

This project was developed through collaboration between human developers and
AI assistance (Claude by Anthropic). The human developer provided:
- Overall system architecture and design
- Language specification and syntax design  
- Technical requirements and feature specifications
- Domain expertise and validation
- Testing scenarios and quality assurance

The AI assistant provided:
- Implementation of specifications in Rust
- Algorithm development based on requirements
- Documentation generation
- Code structure and organization
- Bug fixes and optimizations

This collaborative approach is similar to working with a development team where
different members contribute different expertise. The human developer maintains
creative control, direction, and validation of all work.

## Third-Party Components

This software depends on ~420 Rust crates from crates.io, overwhelmingly
dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. Attributions the licenses ask for, per
`cargo metadata` (regenerate this list when dependencies change; a
`cargo-deny` license gate runs in CI):

- rowan (https://github.com/rust-analyzer/rowan) — Apache-2.0 OR MIT
- nalgebra (https://nalgebra.org/) — BSD-3-Clause
- petgraph (https://github.com/petgraph/petgraph) — Apache-2.0 OR MIT
- tokio (https://tokio.rs/) — MIT
- smartstring (via rhai) — MPL-2.0+ (unmodified; the one MPL crate,
  non-optional under rhai; source at https://crates.io/crates/smartstring)
- yansi — MIT
- ring — Apache-2.0 AND ISC
- rustls-webpki, untrusted, libloading — ISC
- webpki-roots (Mozilla CA bundle) — CDLA-Permissive-2.0
- encoding_rs — (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause
- subtle, zerocopy — BSD-3-Clause / BSD-2-Clause dual forms
- ICU/idna family (18 crates) — Unicode-3.0
- ryu — Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0

smartstring is used unmodified; its source is available at the listed
location per MPL §3.2(b). No GPL/AGPL/LGPL code is linked.

Data provenance: MIL-HDBK-217F reliability constants
(bhdl-stdlib/safety/milhdbk217f.toml) are a US Government work in the
public domain. Proprietary reliability standards (SN 29500, IEC TR 62380,
FIDES) are NOT included — they plug in via gitignored local overlays or
external provider executables. Vendor IBIS models are not redistributed;
`bhdl vendor install` fetches them under the vendors' own terms.

For the complete dependency list and licenses, run `cargo metadata` or
`cargo deny list`.

